# Line-ending and file-type policy.
#
# The repository stores every text file with LF, so the content is identical on every platform and
# diffs stay readable. `text=auto` lets git detect text itself, and `eol=lf` fixes the checkout to LF
# as well — a Windows clone then no longer produces a whole-file diff on the first edit.
#
# Existing files are converted with:
#     git add --renormalize .
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets: never normalised, never diffed as text.
*.mp3  binary
*.wav  binary
*.png  binary
*.bmp  binary
*.ico  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary

# Build products that should never be committed at all (the ignore rules cover them; this is a second
# line of defence if one is added to the index by mistake).
*.dll binary
*.lib binary
*.exe binary
*.obj binary
*.a   binary
